From 200e3101bf80dbf4fe2d64d096a06538dcbbde71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:17:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): dispatcher releases don't earn the
 operator exemption

PR #2923 exempted a card behind a wall with a registered check (default
github-rest-quota) from the running-sibling hold and the probe interval when
the card's own `unblocked` event is newer than its own last assertion, so a
peer cannot revoke an operator's explicit release.

The dispatcher writes the same `unblocked` event when it releases cards
itself: release_cleared_blockers (after a check exits 0) and
probe_stranded_blockers. After a verified recovery, a run that started after
it and finds the quota exhausted again re-asserts the wall, yet every
released card kept passing the exemption, so each spawned once only to
rediscover the wall (26 cards behind this wall on worker-1 on 2026-11-13).

Only an operator release earns the exemption now. `_operator_released`
treats the card's newest `unblocked` event as the dispatcher's when the
card's very next event (portable #2946 order) is shared_blocker_cleared or
shared_blocker_probe_released; such a card falls back to the normal rule,
where a newer assertion by any card holds it. #2923's fence is unchanged: a
stale assertion from a run that began before the recovery still never
re-holds a released card.

Also corrects the fence docstring: run_due_checks runs only while a wall is
open, so after a verified clear only a run that started after the recovery
re-opens it, never the next cheap check.

Cost note: the per-id config reload this card was asked to measure is
already gone on main (0190f3467d snapshots config per blocker pass), so this
commit adds no config cache of its own.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_shared_blocker_release_kinds.py. The
check-release and probe-release cases fail on main (guard returns None) and
pass here; the fence and operator-after-dispatcher cases pass on both. No
existing case pinned the old behaviour; every test file importing the module
passes unmodified.
